{{Quote|You speak terrible Jawa. You sound like a Wookiee.|translated=1|A Jawa, to the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="The Mandalorian 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref>}}
'''Jawaese''',<ref name="AbEverything" /> also referred to simply as '''Jawa''',<ref name="The Mandalorian 2" /> was the original [[language]] of the [[Jawa]]s, while [[Jawa Trade Talk]] was their dialect. Scent was an integral part of Jawaese so it was<ref name="AbEverything" /> near<ref name="Jabbering">{{ArenaNews|url=6df609ffb43d48398e94a37c9a75aa88-en-gb|text=Jabbering in Jawaese}}</ref> impossible for non-Jawas to learn.<ref name="AbEverything" /> The language had no word for "cowardice." There were twenty-seven words for "junk" in Jawaese.<ref name="Survival Instinct">{{Destiny|set=Covert Missions|cardname=Survival Instinct|link=https://swdestinydb.com/card/12136}}</ref>

The [[Bimm]] weapons [[smuggler]] [[Rycar Ryjerd]] spoke Jawaese.<ref name="CL2016" />

==Examples==
{{Quote|For those of you at home, Jawaese is not easy to learn for non-Jawas. Part of the language itself involves emitting and detecting certain scents. Hence in some cases, I am only able to offer limited translations.|[[L-X1]]|<ref name="Jabbering" />}}
*''Ibana'' ("Yes")<ref name="SWTVE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>
*''Monasuka'' ("egg")<ref name="The Mandalorian 2" />
*''M'um m'aloo'' ("Hello")<ref name="SWTVE" />
*''Nyeta'' ("No")<ref name="SWTVE" />
*''Taa baa'' ("Thank you")<ref name="SWTVE" />
*''Togo Togu!'' ("Hands off!")<ref name="SWTVE" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the films, Jawaese was produced by speeding up words and phrases spoken in the [[Wikipedia:Zulu language|Zulu language]].<ref name="Creatures+Aliens">''[[The Moviemaking Magic of Star Wars: Creatures & Aliens]]''</ref>

